		"why": "A loop keeps them going; the if decides what to do each time."},
	"Teamwork: waiter and cook": {"q": "How does a waiter hand an order to the cook?",
		"a": ["By posting it on the counter", "By shouting", "By using a comment"], "ok": 0,
		"why": "The waiter posts the order; the cook checks the counter for tickets."},
	"Your Level 3 challenges": {"q": "Which loop is best when you know the exact count?",
		"a": ["for", "do / while", "switch"], "ok": 0,
		"why": "for keeps the start, condition and update together, perfect for counting."},
	# --- Lesson 4 -------------------------------------------------------------------
	"What is an array?": {"q": "An array stores...",
		"a": ["Many values of the same type", "Only one letter", "Comments"], "ok": 0,
